# Keep a task apart from a docked module of the same name, for the backends where the two cannot share one.
#
# `native/<platform>/log.tree` docks its runtime module as `log` and calls `log/write-warn`, and `console` defines a
# task `log`. Rust holds both (a module and a function live in different namespaces), and TypeScript emits the dock
# under its import. Swift refuses `enum log` beside `func log` ("invalid redeclaration"), and Kotlin reads `log.writeInfo`
# on the function `log`. So a program loading `console`'s `log` beside `log`'s `warn` built on node and Rust and failed
# on Swift and Kotlin (guides: library/processes, 2026-10-04).
#
# The task is renamed, never the module: the module's name is its runtime shim's, fixed in the prelude. A reference is
# renamed where it is a call's callee or the checker bound it to the task (`binding.kind` 'function'), so a dock
# reference, always the target of a member, keeps its name.
# `__task` cannot collide with a Term name, which never holds an underscore.
#
# Ported from compile/dock-apart.ts (self-hosting, 2026-10-05): the renaming is compile/node-rewrite's `rename-tasks`
# rule, over a copy of the program, since the emitter that asks is handed the program every backend shares.

load @term/base/list
  find list

load @term/base/maybe
  find maybe

load ./node
  find statement

load ./node-rewrite
  find rewrite-rule
  find rewrite-program
  find copy-program

task keep-docks-apart
  take program, like list, like statement
  like list, like statement

  save docks, make list
  walk program
    take one
    sift one
      case native
        save is-type, false
        sift kind
          case some
            link given
            sift given
              case type
                save is-type, true
              case module
                save is-type, false
          case none
            save is-type, false
        fork test, not(is-type)
          hold
            push(docks, alias)
      miss
        turn next

  save clashing, make list
  walk program
    take one
    sift one
      case function
        fork test, and(has-text(docks, name), not(has-text(clashing, name)))
          hold
            push(clashing, name)
      miss
        turn next

  fork test, is-equal(clashing/length, 0)
    hold
      back program

  save rule
    make rename-tasks
      bind names, clashing
      bind suffix, <__task>
  back rewrite-program(copy-program(program), rule)

task has-text
  take values, like list, like text
  take value, like text
  like boolean
  mark private

  walk values
    take one
    fork test, is-equal(one, value)
      hold
        back true
  back false
